    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_body">PK Tracker estimates how substances rise and fall in the body from population-average pharmacokinetic models. It is a quantified-self tool, not a medical device.</string>
    <string name="version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="download_latest">Download latest release</string>
    <string name="whats_new">What\'s new</string>
    <string name="changelog_2_5_0">2.5.0 — Sign in with Google (Settings → Cloud sync): link your anonymous account to your Google identity so your log follows you across devices and reinstalls.</string>
    <string name="changelog_2_4_0">2.4.0 — Cloud sync (opt-in, Settings → Cloud sync): your dose log now syncs across your devices through your private Firebase account, with anonymous sign-in.</string>
    <string name="changelog_2_3_0">2.3.0 — Home-screen widget: shows your active substance\'s current level in its own colour, plus time since your last dose. Tap to open; refreshes after every dose.</string>
    <string name="changelog_2_2_0">2.2.0 — Smart reminders (opt-in): model-timed nudges like the last coffee before your sleep cutoff, or a redose when focus dips — never generic. Plus groundwork for cross-device sync.</string>
    <string name="changelog_2_1_0">2.1.0 — Stimulants (Ritalin, Concerta, Vyvanse, Adderall) now get a sleep-cutoff card too, based on each drug\'s own threshold. Plus cards now animate in as the screen assembles.</string>
    <string name="changelog_2_0_0">2.0.0 — A big redesign: every substance now themes the whole dashboard in its own colour, a live gauge headlines your current level, and a new Insights tab shows when you have it, your weekly rhythm, and averages. Plus a curve-based logo and animations throughout.</string>
    <string name="changelog_1_0_4">1.0.4 — Added this download link and changelog, so you can always find and check the latest build from inside the app.</string>
    <string name="changelog_1_0_3">1.0.3 — Brand-name drug labels (Ritalin/Attent, Concerta, Vyvanse, Adderall), a chart with real axes you can pan through past and future, more Hebrew coverage.</string>
    <string name="changelog_1_0_2">1.0.2 — Fixed a crash on launch.</string>
    <string name="changelog_1_0_1">1.0.1 — Accessibility and translation polish.</string>
    <string name="disclaimer">Estimates only — not medical advice. Individual metabolism varies widely. Never use alcohol figures to decide whether to drive.</string>

